TI  - Agricultural soil moisture monitoring using scatterometers
PY  - 2025
T2  - Earth Observation using Scatterometers: State-of-the-Art Techniques, Applications, and Challenges
SP  - 237
EP  - 254
DO  - 10.1016/B978-0-443-31380-6.00001-5
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105026832632?origin=resultslist
AB  - Agricultural soil moisture (SM) monitoring is critical for sustainable cultivation and addressing environmental challenges. Recent advances in scatterometer (SCAT) technology have enhanced the accuracy and efficiency of SM monitoring. SCAT devices are a perfect solution for remote sensing applications. Integrating SM data from SCATs into hydrological models has also demonstrated promising outcomes in simulations and improved calibration models. This chapter discusses the applications and importance of SCAT in remote SM monitoring for informed agricultural decision-making. This chapter discusses applications of SCAT technology and for SM monitoring to to enhance precision agriculture practices, improve water management techniques, mitigate deficit water risks, and optimize crop yields. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved..
