TI  - Role of AI and IoT in agricultural applications using Google Earth Engine
PY  - 2025
T2  - Google Earth Engine and Artificial Intelligence for Earth Observation: Algorithms and Sustainable Applications
SP  - 449
EP  - 464
DO  - 10.1016/B978-0-443-27372-8.00026-X
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105011241826?origin=resultslist
AB  - Precision agriculture incorporates advanced technologies to improve the ways and efficiency of farming. The study aims at describing how both GEE and machine learning contribute to precision agriculture, particularly, information management in agriculture. GEE, with its database including hundreds of thousands of satellite images and geospatial data, plays an essential role of a complete diagnostic system for crops condition, the state of the soils, and the effect of the climate. Artificial intelligence builds up on this proficiency due to the capacity of machine learning algorithms to predict as well as classify the features of agriculture. First, integration of rainfall estimation as well as soil moisture data from scatterometer data augments the study by supplying detailed information on the partly required attribute for irrigation and optimal crop yield. The use of Internet of Things (IoT) devices supports this strategy by providing time. Concrete and measurable benefits that support this approach are as follows. Due to its ability to monitor and control conditions such as temperature, relative humidity, and nutrient available to plant roots on a constant basis effective response to the changing environment can be made instantly. This chapter demonstrates the correlation of GEE, machine learning, scatterometer data, and IoT devices in developing a precision agriculture model that optimizes productivity. The incorporation of these aforementioned technologies is expected to bring a dramatic change to the agricultural activities through the notion of efficient farming, using resources appropriately and productivity improvement of crops. © 2025 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
