AB  - In the Sahel region, an extension of Precision agriculture (PA) is imparted to address the issues emerging out of soil health and climate change. This paper studies PA techniques that use technology and data analysis to improve agricultural production systems. PA, through remote sensing, GPS, and data analysis, allows a farmer to irrigate, fertilise, manage pests, and treat crops according to their needs and soil conditions, thereby fourfold preventing the waste of resources, nu-trient leaching, and soil erosion. In a semi-arid region where water is limited, PA becomes critically useful for proper water management in the delivery of optimal soil moisture to the crops. PA centers on furthering soil structure and retention mechanisms of nutrients for sustainable crop production and soil health. PA thus provides swift transformations in this perspective, in contrast to initiatives fostered for resilience by climate change. Precise information regarding water availability, climate variability, and adjustments to crop management practices will help reduce vulnerability to climate change. Building production and resilience through PA in semi-arid areas, therefore, holds results for sustainability. Farmer capacity development and conducive policy implementation hence are imperatives towards technology adoption. © 2025, Scibulcom Ltd.. All rights reserved.
