AB  - In modern conditions, irrigated agriculture allows efficient use of land and water due to limited land and water resources, increase soil fertility through rational use of fertilizers, obtain a high planned and sustainable yield of agricultural products, and take care of the natural environment. Based on the literature analysis, we can conclude that intelligent irrigation management methods meet all the requirements of modern irrigated agriculture and have the advantage of maximally automating the process of irrigation and soil mineralization. This is evidenced by the widespread use of this irrigation method in the USA, Israel, New Zealand, Iran, etc. Therefore, at the present stage, the development of an automated control system for intelligent irrigation management methods is becoming relevant, providing for the management of the main factors of productivity, taking into account the variability of natural and climatic conditions of agriculture in Uzbekistan to achieve high levels of productivity, exceeding the existing ones by 2-4 times. The goal of the algorithm based on fuzzy logic is to determine the timing and amount of water and mineral delivery, taking into account the information provided by a real-time wireless monitoring system of the agro-climatic environmental conditions. This system is based on measurement devices (using sensors for soil moisture, air temperature, solar radiation, etc.) and data obtained from the growth and development model of agricultural crop biomass, as well as from a satellite-based geoinformation system. The collected data are used as input variables for the fuzzy logic system, which determines the timing and amount for mineralized irrigation. © 2025 Author(s).
