AB  - This study presents an integrated, intelligent solution for smart gardening that synergizes Internet of Things (IoT), cloud computing, and blockchain technologies to automate and optimize plant irrigation. By using a network of embedded sensors to continuously monitor soil moisture and nutrient levels, the suggested system allows for real-time evaluation of environmental conditions and plant health. Through an easy-to-use user interface, the Amazon Web Services (AWS) Cloud processes and analyses the data collected by the sensors to enable remote decision-making and dynamic irrigation control. Every sensor reading and system action is permanently documented on a blockchain ledger to guarantee the accuracy, safety, and openness of environmental data. In addition to facilitating effective water use and enhancing crop management, its dual-layer architecture offers a tamperproof audit trail of resource consumption and environmental conditions. The suggested framework provides a safe and scalable method of smart agriculture that might greatly improve resilience and sustainability in gardening ecosystems in both urban and rural areas. © 2025 IEEE.
