AB  - Most stocks and crops are grown in open field environments. An important factor for crop growth in such outdoor cultivation is irrigation. In the case of conventional irrigation systems, which are mostly based on soil moisture content and weather conditions, crops suffer from over-or under-watering problems. Under these circumstances, many researchers are conducting research on irrigation systems based on crop information such as leaf temperature. In this paper, we propose a smart irrigation system that analyzes the CWSI of crops based on the leaf temperature of the crops to determine the amount of irrigation. The results of this paper can be useful in determining the irrigation timing andIt is expected that it will be possible to solve the problem of difficulty in occupying farmland area and Equipment Retention which is a disadvantage of the existing CWSI calculation applying  © 2023 IEEE.
