DO  - 10.1109/ICCCNT61001.2024.10724140
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85212925216?origin=resultslist
AB  - This paper aims to address the pressing challenges faced by farmers in modern agriculture by introducing an innovative Artificial Intelligence(AI)-Driven Farm Management System, the latest solution that leverages predictive analytics, geo-integrated monitoring, a chatbot similar to GPT, and resource allocation to optimize agricultural operations and enhance overall productivity. Through geo-integrated monitoring, real-time data from various sources such as remote sensors, weather forecasts, satellite imagery is analyzed to enable precise monitoring of crop health, soil moisture levels, and weather patterns. The system provides farmers with valuable insights and data-driven recommendations for decision-making, helping them anticipate and mitigate potential risks while maximizing yields. Additionally, resource allocation algorithms allocate resources such as water, fertilizers, and pesticides in an efficient and sustainable manner, reducing waste and environmental impact. The platform is designed with a user-friendly interface using Streamlit, allowing farmers to easily access and interact with the data and insights generated. The system empowers farmers with real-time field monitoring, data-driven decision-making, resource optimization, predictive planning, and improved crop yields. The motivation stems from the need for modern tools to enhance farm efficiency and productivity, ultimately addressing the evolving challenges in agriculture. By harnessing the power of AI and farm management processes, this system empowers farmers to make informed decisions and optimize their operations for increased profitability and sustainability. © 2024 IEEE.
